.TH L10N-LINT 1 "February 2026" "l10n-lint 1.15.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
l10n-lint \- linter for localization files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B l10n-lint
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B l10n-lint
checks gettext .po and Qt .ts localization files for common issues:
missing translations, fuzzy entries, placeholder mismatches, length problems, 
and other translation quality issues. It supports direct GitHub repository
analysis and various output formats for integration with different workflows.

The tool performs comprehensive checks including: missing translations detection,
fuzzy entry identification, placeholder consistency validation, translation
length ratio analysis, maximum length enforcement, and format string verification.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message with usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version number and build information, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-g " " \fIREPO\fR ", " \-\-github " " \fIREPO\fR
Analyze a GitHub repository directly without cloning locally.
Specify as owner/repo (e.g., "yeager/l10n-lint") or as a full URL.
Automatically discovers and scans all supported translation files
in the repository using the GitHub API.
.TP
.BR \-p " " \fIPATH\fR ", " \-\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Path filter for GitHub repositories. When used with \-\-github,
limits scanning to specific subdirectories within the repository.
Supports glob patterns for flexible path matching.
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFORMAT\fR ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format for the lint report. Available formats:
.RS 8
.B text
(default) Human-readable text format with colored output
.RE
.RS 8
.B json
Machine-readable JSON format for programmatic processing
.RE
.RS 8
.B html
HTML report suitable for web browsers with interactive features
.RE
.RS 8
.B github
GitHub Actions annotation format for CI/CD integration
.RE
.RS 8
.B gnu
Emacs-compatible file:line:col format for editor integration
.RE
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIFILE\fR ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Save the lint report to the specified file instead of writing to stdout.
The file format is automatically detected from the extension if no
\-\-format is specified.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-length " " \fIN\fR
Maximum allowed translation length in characters (default: 500).
Translations exceeding this limit are flagged as potentially
problematic for UI layout. Set to 0 to disable length checking.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-recursive
Do not recursively search subdirectories for translation files.
Only process files directly specified or in the immediate directory.
Useful for controlled scanning of large directory structures.
.TP
.BR \-\-strict
Treat all warnings as errors. When enabled, the exit code will be
non-zero even for minor issues that would normally be warnings.
This is useful for enforcing strict translation quality in CI pipelines.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode. Show only the final summary line with total counts.
Suppress all detailed per-file output and progress indicators.
Individual issue details are not displayed.
.TP
.BR \-\-check
Check-only mode for CI/CD integration. Perform the complete analysis
but produce absolutely no output - communicate results only through
the exit code. Useful for automated quality gates.
.TP
.BR \-\-skip\-fuzzy
Skip fuzzy translation entry checks. Fuzzy entries are normally
flagged as incomplete translations requiring review, but this
option ignores them during analysis. Useful when fuzzy entries
are expected or acceptable in the current workflow.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output with detailed progress information.
Shows timing data, file sizes, locale detection results,
per-file issue counts, and other diagnostic information
useful for debugging and performance analysis.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-gtk
Launch the GTK4 graphical user interface instead of running
in command-line mode. The GUI provides interactive file browsing,
real-time results, and visual issue highlighting. Note: This
option launches a GUI application, not a CLI tool.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No translation issues found. All files passed validation.
.TP
.B 1
Translation issues detected, or an error occurred during processing.
The specific issues are detailed in the output (unless using \-\-check).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check all translation files in current directory recursively:
.B l10n-lint .
.TP
Check specific .po file with detailed output:
.B l10n-lint \-\-verbose messages.po
.TP
Generate JSON report for CI integration:
.B l10n-lint \-\-format json \-\-output report.json src/
.TP
Check GitHub repository directly:
.B l10n-lint \-\-github yeager/l10n-lint
.TP
Check specific path in GitHub repo:
.B l10n-lint \-\-github user/repo \-\-path "locale/"
.TP
Strict checking with custom length limit:
.B l10n-lint \-\-strict \-\-max-length 200 *.po
.TP
Skip fuzzy entries, quiet output:
.B l10n-lint \-\-skip-fuzzy \-\-quiet po/
.TP
Generate HTML report:
.B l10n-lint \-\-format html \-\-output report.html locale/
.TP
GNU format for Emacs integration:
.B l10n-lint \-\-format gnu translations/
.TP
CI-friendly check (exit code only):
.B l10n-lint \-\-check src/locale/
.SH CHECKS PERFORMED
.B l10n-lint
performs the following validation checks:
.TP
.B Missing Translations
Identifies untranslated strings that should have translations.
.TP
.B Fuzzy Entries
Flags translations marked as fuzzy (requiring review).
.TP
.B Placeholder Mismatches
Validates that format specifiers (%s, %d, etc.) match between
original and translated strings.
.TP
.B Length Ratio Analysis
Checks if translations are significantly longer or shorter
than the original text (may indicate translation issues).
.TP
.B Maximum Length Validation
Ensures translations don't exceed the specified character limit
(useful for UI constraints).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B *.po
GNU gettext portable object files
.TP
.B *.ts
Qt Linguist translation source files
